rota lap 4684, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; the threshold page names three wrong readings a lap should take in whole at the door -- a stamp outrunning the live clock, a page whose status names no room, a value crossing a seam unmarked. Two were already closed: the doorway scan reads living_silent=0 and 124 living pages carrying a Last updated line read 0 in the future. So the row sent me to a fourth door it does not name -- the first line of a module.
think Reds first. Cold roster pass launched with --detach; two reds stood at the close of my reading, and neither was a tree fault of this lap's making: remember_git_nib went red the moment my claim commit moved HEAD past the card's pinned nib, and this round's work commit carries the nib forward; glow_run_contract is PHEROMONE's landed contract wanting a rebuilt binary. dated_path stays parked at %626 wanting a gate word.
think The earth threshold asks for the concrete fact read at the door before any argument. Gauge runs its dial through the code -- Meter beside a bound, Door at the head of a module -- and Zig writes Door into the grammar: //! is accepted only at the top of a file. So the door is a position rather than a habit.
think tools/fixtures/c/comment_dial_scan.sh has counted that form since 20260824 and gates nothing, by its own header's deliberate choice. The reading stood eighteen days and no lap met it: 1,963 of 1,973 authored modules open with //!, nine open with an ordinary // block, one opens with code.
obs The nine were not doorless, which is the finding. Eight carried real Door prose in the form the compiler does not reserve -- a WHY paragraph, a list of commands and the log behind them -- so a reader met a door and every tool read a wall. The tenth carried its prose inside main, where the sentence answers nobody arriving at the file.
obs All ten paths repaired, and they are nine files: the three font8x8_data.rye entries are one table reached by two symlinks, which the tracked listing reports as three paths. The reading counts paths, which is right for a meter asking whether a reader arriving at a path meets a door. The four that build as programs were rebuilt on metal through rye/bin/rye build; the table keeps its attribution line word for word with only the marker moved, proven through its importer by tools/h/hunk_skate_witness.rish reading GREEN.
obs A second instrument rather than a widened first one. comment_dial keeps its scope -- a measurement is finished when its question is answered -- and the wall gets its own scan, control and witness.
obs Three refusals the control taught. A rule spelled twice drifts: the exempt classes were found by a grep and the remainder by the matching inverse grep, and the widening mutation moved only one copy, so the complement is taken with comm now. A dead line kept answering: gated was computed twice, agreeing on the living tree by arithmetic accident and reading -1 in the pen. And a mutation that no longer applies reads exactly like one that passed, so every mutation leg asserts applied before it asserts bites.
obs Cost decided the shape. One grep per module is 1,911 processes and 27 seconds; one awk over the gated corpus reads the same tree in one. A lap-tier guard has to be affordable or it becomes a cadence tier -- which is the shape this reading exists to refuse, since there a stranger repairs somebody else's door five rounds later.
